cited_sources.excerpt:
Today, we lack principled ways to assess the quality of tool calling decisions made by LLM agents.
Most evaluations are coarse-grained—they test whether tool calling improves the aggregate accuracy (Yao et al., 2023; Qian et al., 2025; Feng et al., 2025)—and overlook finer-grained aspects of performance.
The lack of such assessments makes it difficult to investigate principled approaches to enhance (improve) agentic decisions to call tools. [...] al., 2024; Singh et al., 2025; Qian et al., 2025;

